# Default profiles to ignore (known-noisy or expected profiles).
# Supports glob patterns (e.g. *claude-code*).
# These are merged into /var/lib/apparmor-monitor/ignore-profiles on install/update.
# Add your own entries directly to the installed file -- they won't be removed.
snap.firmware-updater.firmware-notifier
snap.snapd-desktop-integration.snapd-desktop-integration
# snap-confine reading /run/gdm3 during GDM-greeter snap launches (read-only,
# benign — the snap works regardless). Same greeter cluster as firmware-notifier
# above. snapd reports this profile under TWO paths: the versioned snap one
# (/snap/snapd/<rev>/usr/lib/snapd/snap-confine), which changes on every refresh,
# and the deb-installed /usr/lib/snapd/snap-confine that runs before the snap
# re-exec takes over — byte-identical denial, so a rev-pinned or /snap-anchored
# pattern leaks the second form. One leading-* glob covers both and still does
# not match /usr/bin/snap-confine or a suffixed name. Verified against both
# consumers (check_violations' awk glob→regex and check_tamper's python fnmatch).
*/usr/lib/snapd/snap-confine
